From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH perf 005] kbase: cache the kbase_kmod_bo wrapper structs

Every pan_kmod_bo_alloc()/alloc_dmabuf()/import() allocated a
kbase_kmod_bo through the device allocator, and every final pan_kmod_bo_put()
freed it again. BOs come and go constantly (command buffers, descriptor
pools, transient images), so the wrapper struct is a per-BO allocator round
trip that buys nothing.

Keep up to KBASE_BO_CACHE_MAX free wrappers per device in a list and reuse
them. Only the host-side struct is pooled: the GPU memory itself is still
allocated/imported and freed through the kernel on every create/destroy, so
the driver's memory semantics, including the kernel's deferred reclaim of
GPU pages, are untouched. kbase_kmod_bo_wrapper_alloc() zeroes a reused
wrapper (the previous BO's fields must not leak into the new one).

Purpose: remove one allocator alloc/free pair per BO.
Tested GPU: build only, not yet run on device.
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21, JM 11.x.
Mesa base range: 26.3.0-devel (pinned 5a07217f).
Dependencies: perf/004 (same file).
Validation test: TBD, on-device render smoke test.

Generated-by: LLM

